fr:mainmatter.html:p:
"Strings are tiny" is the statement that \texttt {String}\, w \otimes  {\mathopen {}\left (-\right )\mathclose {}}
carries two right adjoints in sequence — the derivative, then the
amazing right adjoint.

fr:mainmatter.fr:tex:
\frac {A \And  X \;\vdash \; B}{X \;\vdash \; A \Rightarrow  B}\;{\mathopen {}\left (\Rightarrow ,\ \mathrm {inv.}\right )\mathclose {}}
\qquad 
\frac {A \otimes  X \;\vdash \; B}{X \;\vdash \; A \multimap  B}\;{\mathopen {}\left (\multimap ,\ \mathrm {inv.}\right )\mathclose {}}

\frac {\texttt {String}\, w \otimes  X \;\vdash \; B}{X \;\vdash \; D_w B}\;{\mathopen {}\left (D,\ \mathrm {inv.}\right )\mathclose {}}
\qquad 
\frac {D_w X \;\vdash \; C}{X \;\vdash \; \sqrt [w]{C}}\;{\mathopen {}\left (\surd ,\ \mathrm {inv.}\right )\mathclose {}}

\frac {\rhd  C \;\vdash \; C}{\top  \;\vdash \; C}\;{\mathopen {}\left (\mathrm {L\ddot  ob}\right )\mathclose {}}
\qquad 
\frac {\rhd  C \;\vdash \; C}{I \;\vdash \; C}\;{\mathopen {}\left (\mathrm {L\ddot  ob}_I\right )\mathclose {}}

\frac {A \And  \rhd {\mathopen {}\left (A \Rightarrow  B\right )\mathclose {}} \;\vdash \; B}{A \;\vdash \; B}\;{\mathopen {}\left (\mathrm {Open}\right )\mathclose {}}
\qquad 
\frac {A \otimes  \rhd {\mathopen {}\left (A \multimap  B\right )\mathclose {}} \;\vdash \; B}{A \;\vdash \; B}\;{\mathopen {}\left (\mathrm {L\ddot  ob}_\otimes \right )\mathclose {}}

\cfrac {
